Title: Name the directory and the reason when it cannot be created
Repository: libresprite
Base: 89ea7597ed1d779e85c0019555f5b97c7eac22f0
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-16
Author: aros-libresprite project
Problem: "Error creating directory" did not say which directory or why.
Change: Add the path and strerror(errno) to the message.
Scope: all platforms
Upstream: candidate
Verification: Built for mainline AROS x86_64 (GCC 10.5, SDK nightly 20261110); LibreSprite starts on nightly 20261113 (pool v1-1, 2026-11-16)
Removal: When upstream reports the path and reason.
---
diff --git a/src/base/fs_unix.h b/src/base/fs_unix.h
index ed3fd00ed1f1c10423680116ad58d704c32eceb5..cbff9527282c41668e81a2c963c0c09eed0b892d 100644
--- a/src/base/fs_unix.h
+++ b/src/base/fs_unix.h
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 #include <sys/types.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
 
+#include <cerrno>
 #include <climits>              // Required for PATH_MAX
 #include <cstdio>               // Required for rename()
 #include <cstdlib>
@@ -57,8 +58,7 @@ void make_directory(const std::string& path)
 {
   int result = mkdir(path.c_str(), 0777);
   if (result < 0) {
-    // TODO add errno into the exception
-    throw std::runtime_error("Error creating directory");
+    throw std::runtime_error("Error creating directory " + path + ": " + strerror(errno));
   }
 }
 
